    "finding": "013-byday-mixed-signed-and-unsigned",
    "note": "A BYDAY list mixing a signed weekdaynum with an unsigned one is a union of its elements, not an intersection. RFC 5545 3.3.10's own example FREQ=MONTHLY;INTERVAL=2;COUNT=10;BYDAY=1SU,-1SU expands to the first *and* the last Sunday, and 'BYDAY=MO ... represents all Mondays within the month'; nothing in 3.3.10 makes the elements of the list constrain each other. python-dateutil 2.9.0.post0 splits BYDAY into _byweekday (unsigned) and _bynweekday (signed) and then applies the two as separate exclusion clauses, so a day must match both -- yielding an empty recurrence set when the weekdays differ. Its own BYMONTHDAY handling, three lines below in the same condition, gets the signed/unsigned union right. See finding 013.",
    "verdict": "naive"
   },
